{"book":9,"chapter":2,"context":{"chapter":2,"title":"Hannah's Song, Eli's Sons","summary":"Hannah praises the God who humbles the proud and lifts the poor. Meanwhile Eli's sons, Hophni and Phinehas, abuse their priestly office, and a man of God announces the downfall of Eli's family. Young Samuel keeps growing in favor.","background":"Hannah's song closely resembles Mary's song in Luke 1:46-55, and it already speaks of God's 'king' and 'anointed' (v. 10) before Israel had a king. The law said the fat of a sacrifice belonged to God and was burned first, with the priests receiving set portions (Leviticus 7:31-34); Eli's sons took what they wanted, by force.","customs":[{"term":"Fleshhook","verses":"2:13-14","note":"A three-pronged fork plunged into the boiling pot. Whatever it brought up, the priest's servant took."},{"term":"Exalt the horn","verses":"2:1-10","note":"A horn, as on a strong ox, pictured strength and honor."}],"watchFor":["The great reversals: the full go hungry, the barren bear children (vv. 4–8).","Samuel's growth alternates with the sons' sins (vv. 11–26); verse 26 is echoed of Jesus in Luke 2:52.","'Them that honour me I will honour' (v. 30)."],"connections":["Leviticus 7:31-34","Luke 1:46-55","Luke 2:52","1 Kings 2:27"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַתִּתְפַּלֵּל","vatitpalel","H6419","Hc/Vtw3fs","and she prayed"],["חַנָּה","chanah","H2584","HNpf","Hannah"],["וַתֹּאמַר","vatomar","H559","Hc/Vqw3fs","and she said"],["עָלַץ","'alatz","H5970","HVqp3ms","it rejoices"],["לִבִּי","libi","H3820","HNcmsc/Sp1bs","heart my"],["בַּיהוָה","bayahweh","H3068","HR/Npt","in Yahweh"],["רָמָה","ramah","H7311","HVqp3fs","it is exalted"],["קַרְנִי","karni","H7161","HNcfsc/Sp1bs","horn my"],["בַּיהוָה","bayahweh","H3068","HR/Npt","in Yahweh"],["רָחַב","rachav","H7337","HVqp3ms","it has opened wide"],["פִּי","pi","H6310","HNcmsc/Sp1bs","mouth my"],["עַל","'al-","H5921","HR","on"],["אוֹיְבַי","'oyvai","H341","HVqrmpc/Sp1bs","enemies my"],["כִּי","ki","H3588","HTc","for"],["שׂ